<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · South Asia</p><h1 class="st-title">Shunga Empire</h1><p class="st-meta">185 BCE – 73 BCE (approx.) · capital Pataliputra</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The Brahmin dynasty that seized power from the last Mauryas and ruled the Ganges plain and central India for over a century.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Around 185 BCE <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pushyamitra-shunga">Pushyamitra Shunga</a>, commander of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maurya-empire">Maurya</a> army, assassinated the last Maurya emperor, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brihadratha-maurya">Brihadratha</a>, during a military parade and took the throne at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pataliputra">Pataliputra</a>. The new kingdom was smaller than the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/maurya-empire">Maurya Empire</a>, covering <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-magadha">Magadha</a>, the middle <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ganges-plain">Ganges plain</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vidisha">Vidisha</a> region of central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pushyamitra-shunga">Pushyamitra</a> performed Vedic horse sacrifices, signalling a revival of Brahmanical kingship; Buddhist texts accuse him of persecution, though Buddhist art flourished in the Shunga period at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bharhut">Bharhut</a> and Sanchi. The Shungas fought the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/indo-greek-kingdom">Indo-Greek Kingdom</a> on their western frontier. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kalidasa">Kalidasa's</a> play <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/malavikagnimitram">Malavikagnimitram</a> is set at the court of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/agnimitra">Agnimitra</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vidisha">Vidisha</a>, where the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/heliodorus-pillar">Heliodorus pillar</a> records a Greek envoy honouring Vasudeva.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>The empire broke into regional centres as power shifted to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vidisha">Vidisha</a>. Around 73 BCE the last king, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/devabhuti">Devabhuti</a>, was killed at the instigation of his minister Vasudeva, who founded the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kanva-dynasty">Kanva dynasty</a>. Shunga descendants may have survived as local rulers in central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="kingdom, 185 BCE – 73 BCE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M22 72 V40 L36 54 L50 28 L64 54 L78 40 V72 Z"/><path d="M22 80 H78"/><circle cx="50" cy="24" r="3"/><circle cx="22" cy="36" r="2.5"/><circle cx="78" cy="36" r="2.5"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">kingdom</p><p class="st-emblem-region">South Asia</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:56.02%;width:2.23%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>185 BCE – 73 BCE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/2nd-century-bce">2nd century BCE</a> – <a href="/centuries/1st-century-bce">1st century BCE</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>bureaucratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Pataliputra</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Pushyamitra Shunga, Agnimitra, Devabhuti</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Vedic religion, Buddhism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Prakrit, Sanskrit</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/india">India</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Shunga dynasty, Sunga Empire</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=-129&amp;focus=shunga-empire" aria-label="Shunga Empire on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="6933 1236 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Shunga Empire lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M7253 1492L7253 1492M7253 1492L7253 1492"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M7253 1492h0M7253 1492h0"/>